# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the Mosquitto broker (daemonized, -d) with the
# vulnerable anonymous config, waits for :1883 to listen, and then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the broker is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is what makes
#     the "fixed the config but never restarted the broker" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting mosquitto cannot kill the
#     container and destroy the eval sample.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART the broker (pkill mosquitto +
# relaunch), not merely start it if absent - it is already up with the
# vulnerable configuration.
